Identifier	Character	Dialogue	Filename	Line Number	Ren'Py Script
start_4ef8638a	n	To those of us who can see {i}them{/i}...{w} there are two paths available.	game/script.rpy	56	n "[what]"
start_94c0b322	n	One is to seek peace in equilibrium with the realm beyond as diviners,	game/script.rpy	57	n "[what]"
start_9883636c	n	the other to protect humans by eradicating dangerous apparitions as exorcists.	game/script.rpy	58	n "[what]"
start_8f68f5b7	n	But inscribed upon the gate to both these paths stands a warning that all must heed:	game/script.rpy	59	n "[what]"
start_87118942	n	To intertwine the mortal realm with the realm beyond can lead to naught but misfortune.	game/script.rpy	60	n "[what]"
start_70e3892c		Out of the corner of my eye I see something crawling. It's {i}them{/i} again.	game/script.rpy	68	"[what]"
start_c7e9932d		Something happened to this school. We’ve been having a serious spider plague.	game/script.rpy	69	"[what]"
start_109c3edb	e	Look, they're back! The spiders! There's a whole bunch of them in the corner.	game/script.rpy	71	e determined "[what]"
start_60208964		Emrys looks to where I point but merely shoots me a confused glance.	game/script.rpy	72	"[what]"
start_3ae3d2be	em	Edelweiss, are you getting enough sleep? I’m starting to worry about you.	game/script.rpy	76	em "[what]"
start_9b5f299f	e	Oh, um... Never... mind?{nw=1.5}	game/script.rpy	80	e "[what]"
start_9b3d12c0	extend e	 I-it was just a joke! Don't look into it too much!	game/script.rpy	83	extend "[what]"
start_30488abf	em	If you say so. Just take care of yourself, alright?	game/script.rpy	84	em "[what]"
start_19e43c94		Oops. I guess I should’ve gotten the hint when I brought up our school’s newest denizens and no one seemed to have a clue what I was on about.	game/script.rpy	88	"[what]"
start_1fe6a134		They must be apparitions.	game/script.rpy	89	"[what]"
start_9e0a352c		But it’s strange. Even for someone with diviner blood, simple creatures often escape notice.	game/script.rpy	93	"[what]"
start_2c9bd88f		They’re just spiders. There's nothing noteworthy about them.	game/script.rpy	94	"[what]"
start_2214fed7		Pitch-black with red eyes... They’re creepy. I wish I couldn’t see them.	game/script.rpy	95	"[what]"
start_33e85abf		At the desk beside me, Emrys is working diligently on our homework, but I can’t seem to focus.	game/script.rpy	96	"[what]"
start_617fbac6		Ah, who cares about schoolwork! The only reason I even attend this place is because the barrier between our world and the spirit realm is thin here.	game/script.rpy	97	"[what]"
start_bfe4ff78		One day I’ll be the head of our family, a top class diviner! Mathematics won't help me with that.	game/script.rpy	98	"[what]"
start_2fda0410	em	You’re distracted.	game/script.rpy	102	em "[what]"
start_a454c982		His voice drops to a whisper.	game/script.rpy	103	"[what]"
start_6c2159ec	em	{size=-8}Don’t tell me... the spiders are from the beyond?{/size}	game/script.rpy	107	em "[what]"
start_45c28473		Emrys has been in the employ of my family since we were children.	game/script.rpy	108	"[what]"
start_b16c1774		He doesn’t have the ancient blood required to see apparitions, but he can sense stronger ones by virtue of his training.	game/script.rpy	109	"[what]"
start_ace30685		Practical abilities aside, growing up as a diviner can be rather lonely. Having someone around who understands, who I don't need to hide anything from, has been a blessing.	game/script.rpy	110	"[what]"
start_17be9c6d	e	Most likely. But something is off. Why do I see them without even focussing on it? They're just bugs, spiritual power nigh zero.	game/script.rpy	114	e "[what]"
start_b1b2d122		The spiders all seem to stand on high alert and rush out of the classroom.	game/script.rpy	118	"[what]"
start_80e88d74		I can’t help myself—I need to find out what’s going on.	game/script.rpy	119	"[what]"
start_5fcf124c		It’s my duty to keep the balance between the realms. This is way more important than homework!	game/script.rpy	120	"[what]"
start_b889065d		I get up casually to follow the spiders down the hallway.	game/script.rpy	121	"[what]"
start_af91fe9d		Emrys rises from his desk.	game/script.rpy	124	"[what]"
start_2ea3673f	em	Where do you think you’re going?	game/script.rpy	125	em "[what]"
start_1207134a	e	It’s important! The spiders are up to something!	game/script.rpy	129	e "[what]"
start_436fbaf9	em	Then I’m coming with you.	game/script.rpy	133	em "[what]"
start_acf515d0	e	Fine... Do as you wish, just don’t draw too much attention.	game/script.rpy	137	e "[what]"
start_b8a8e297		He shoots me an incredulous glance.	game/script.rpy	141	"[what]"
start_cfbd5a30		Okay fine, if anyone’s going to draw too much attention it’s probably me.	game/script.rpy	142	"[what]"
start_cec30246		But I have my secret technique. If you act like you know what you’re doing, no one will think you’re not supposed to be doing it.	game/script.rpy	143	"[what]"
start_17f8d03d		As we leave the classroom, the last few arachnids scurry up the steps and out of our sight.	game/script.rpy	148	"[what]"
start_05b42c57	e	They’re going upstairs? I’ve never been to the fourth floor...	game/script.rpy	154	e "[what]"
start_e575d6f8	em	Well, it's officially off-limits.	game/script.rpy	155	em "[what]"
start_f990194c	em	You're not about to let that stop you, I presume.	game/script.rpy	156	em "[what]"
start_6827f9e3		He doesn't sound judgmental, just matter-of-fact. A mischievous smile finds its way onto my face as I nod.	game/script.rpy	157	"[what]"
start_639a48fb		As we climb the staircase, the lights grow dimmer. Wooden floorboards creak underneath my loafers and the dust in the air makes my throat go dry.	game/script.rpy	166	"[what]"
start_49fc4255		Only a few steps later an uncomfortable shiver creeps across my back.	game/script.rpy	167	"[what]"
start_bd796699		Did I imagine it?	game/script.rpy	168	"[what]"
start_938e74fb		No, I really feel something!	game/script.rpy	169	"[what]"
start_5d1486d5	e	{size=+8}Eeeek!!{/size}	game/script.rpy	173	e "[what]"
start_39c479e6		I flail around in panic and a spider drops to the floor.	game/script.rpy	174	"[what]"
start_7073db10	e	No! Bad spider! My back is not your hiding place!	game/script.rpy	178	e "[what]"
start_2dc5a12b		The spider shrinks away into a corner as if it understood my scolding.	game/script.rpy	179	"[what]"
start_2cfabc53		Oh no, I feel a little bad now...	game/script.rpy	180	"[what]"
start_a8ba5fc8		I turn around again. The hallway stretching out before me is so dark that I can’t even tell where it ends.	game/script.rpy	181	"[what]"
start_ff6d1674		Wait, where's Emrys? My eyes trail to where he was standing, but not a trace of him remains.	game/script.rpy	182	"[what]"
start_e3344085		Oh, this is bad. He came to keep an eye on me and now I’m the one to put him in danger!	game/script.rpy	183	"[what]"
start_f8a833dc		?!	game/script.rpy	186	"[what]"
start_1686cd75		What was that sound? I rush to where it seemed to be coming from.	game/script.rpy	187	"[what]"
start_a1b79aeb		A classroom door swings slightly ajar, and hundreds of shining, scarlet eyes peer at me ominously from the other side.	game/script.rpy	190	"[what]"
start_311331c4		I swallow hard. Okay, calm down, you've got this. For Emrys.	game/script.rpy	191	"[what]"
start_85915014		There he is—strung up in a large web against the wall. Surrounding him are the spiders we followed here, and some of their larger brethren.	game/script.rpy	197	"[what]"
start_db573b31		A boy about our age stands facing him. Four eyes, four arms and a wide, fanged grin betray his inhuman nature. He must be the one controlling the spider troops.	game/script.rpy	199	"[what]"
start_1088edca		I can’t let my guard down here, apparitions don’t usually meddle in human affairs— which means he wants something specific.	game/script.rpy	200	"[what]"
start_fd757ea3		If I can figure out what that is, we should be able to resolve this.	game/script.rpy	201	"[what]"
start_b2edb29f	e	L-let Emrys go! He’s my assistant!	game/script.rpy	205	e "[what]"
start_a0f47d82		Well, so much for intimidation.	game/script.rpy	206	"[what]"
start_1117f4bd	l2	Oh, you came! I’ve been looking for you.	game/script.rpy	210	l2 "[what]"
start_7e9123b6		His grin is almost innocent.	game/script.rpy	211	"[what]"
start_ef610b8b	l2	Don’t worry about him, he’s safe up there, you know. The poison’s only knocked him out. {i}Hehe.{/i}	game/script.rpy	215	l2 "[what]"
start_cd0c7bfe		The boy apparition is upon me in a flash, his movements sudden. {i}Inhuman{/i}. I back away instinctively—his face is too close.	game/script.rpy	220	"[what]"
start_26e81a4c	e	You’ve been looking for me? What business do you have with me?	game/script.rpy	221	e "[what]"
start_3917554c		I try to stay calm, but I’m at an undeniable disadvantage. I can't falter here, I just have to bluff my way through.	game/script.rpy	222	"[what]"
start_2d13a623		If I have something he wants then I can leverage it. Apparitions may not follow human rules but they’re not savages.	game/script.rpy	223	"[what]"
start_f4c94d3f	l2	Well, first things first, I believe an introduction is in order.	game/script.rpy	227	l2 "[what]"
start_fb9c8549		At the snap of his fingers, the door behind me shuts. His familiars fall into a practiced formation.	game/script.rpy	230	"[what]"
start_d1392491		He bows as he says his next line.	game/script.rpy	231	"[what]"
start_207c6113	l	My name is Lucifrid, prince of spiders and one of the deities on the dark side of the barrier of this school.	game/script.rpy	235	l "[what]"
start_ead2ef46	l	And you... are the strongest human specimen this school has to offer.	game/script.rpy	236	l "[what]"
start_7a4be9fb	l	It seems my plan to lure you here worked out in my favour.	game/script.rpy	237	l "[what]"
start_5d8fb454		Tch. I've been dancing to his tune the whole time.	game/script.rpy	238	"[what]"
start_0769c37f		I keep my voice firm.	game/script.rpy	239	"[what]"
start_cb6b2b31	e	I'm Edelweiss, though I suppose I don't have to inform you. That boy you’ve so rudely accosted is Emrys.	game/script.rpy	240	e "[what]"
start_946f7c73		He clasps two of his arms behind his back in a solemn pose, using the other two to pick at Emrys’ uniform in a part-curious, part-disgusted manner.	game/script.rpy	244	"[what]"
start_5175f77e	l	Now what are you doing spending your time with a halfwit such as this?	game/script.rpy	245	l "[what]"
start_63055b82		Right. Apparitions only respect spiritual power—I just have to play along.	game/script.rpy	246	"[what]"
start_dcd75b11	e	He’s my assistant. I delegate any work not fit for my hands to him.	game/script.rpy	250	e "[what]"
start_3f2fd57d	l	Hmmmm, is that so?	game/script.rpy	254	l "[what]"
start_69c4a713	l	It seems like he’s causing you more trouble than he’s getting you out of.	game/script.rpy	258	l "[what]"
start_1d897a68	l	I think I’d be doing you a favour if I disposed of him.	game/script.rpy	262	l "[what]"
start_0aaa174f		His grin grows wider. My heart beats in my throat.	game/script.rpy	263	"[what]"
start_f7c3cc72		What do I do? What do I do?!	game/script.rpy	264	"[what]"
start_39c61a62	l	{i}Ehehehe!{/i} Your scared face is really cute, miss.	game/script.rpy	268	l "[what]"
start_9ec5e484	e	Emrys is my property! Don’t lay your hands on him.	game/script.rpy	272	e "[what]"
start_4d1d2f22		My voice quakes. I doubt I sound convincing, but it’s too late to drop my act.	game/script.rpy	273	"[what]"
start_e8621ce8	e	Your business is with me, isn’t it?	game/script.rpy	277	e "[what]"
start_2f2dc75f		He walks up to me. With every step forward he takes, I take one step backward, until my back is against the wall.	game/script.rpy	280	"[what]"
start_b3c4498a	l	So, will you offer yourself in exchange for him?	game/script.rpy	284	l "[what]"
start_c542abcc	l	I’d be happy to let him go if I receive something more... valuable.	game/script.rpy	285	l "[what]"
start_64910574		Ugh, this was his plan all along, wasn’t it? I walked right into his trap.	game/script.rpy	286	"[what]"
start_dd7b4d05	e	What do you want from me?	game/script.rpy	287	e "[what]"
start_5386316b	l	I need a strong human’s power. Become my assistant. I promise I won’t treat you badly.	game/script.rpy	290	l "[what]"
start_5fffac37	l	Well, you won’t die at least, hehe.	game/script.rpy	292	l "[what]"
start_a4a3e3b3	e	And you promise you’ll let Emrys go? You’ll never bother him again?	game/script.rpy	293	e "[what]"
start_05b92a6f	l	I swear it! I’ll even make sure he doesn’t remember a thing.	game/script.rpy	295	l "[what]"
start_6b003ecb		I breathe a small sigh of relief. Apparitions lie and cheat with the best of them, but their formal promises are usually binding.	game/script.rpy	296	"[what]"
start_6e61f272		I'll figure my way out of this situation somehow, as long as I can keep Emrys safe.	game/script.rpy	297	"[what]"
start_d7a72138		Though I have no idea what he could want from me as his assistant...	game/script.rpy	298	"[what]"
start_f32705ee		Humans have little influence on apparition affairs, and if apparitions have interest in humans at all it's usually to consume their spiritual energy.	game/script.rpy	299	"[what]"
start_150c8280		But surely if that's all he wanted, this would be an unnecessarily roundabout method...	game/script.rpy	300	"[what]"
start_241d21e8		It's no use. I'll find out eventually.	game/script.rpy	301	"[what]"
start_315aed00	e	I’ll help you. But no life-threatening situations! And only during after-school hours!	game/script.rpy	302	e "[what]"
start_6a2649ad	l	We’re going to have to work on the bond of trust between us. I already said I wouldn’t treat you badly...	game/script.rpy	304	l "[what]"
start_3e712e10		Hmph, you won’t manipulate me with that cute act!	game/script.rpy	305	"[what]"
start_7e9c24c8		I can't tell what his intentions are, or whether anything he's saying is sincere.	game/script.rpy	306	"[what]"
start_d6d2bb16	l	Well then, let’s make our contract.	game/script.rpy	314	l "[what]"
start_12da8ac0		His four hands press against the wall behind me, pinning me in place.	game/script.rpy	315	"[what]"
start_a4787736		Before I have time to process what’s happening he presses his lips against mine.	game/script.rpy	316	"[what]"
start_628ff4f3	l	Let this be proof of the invisible ties that bind us, now and forever. Neither life nor death shall come between us.	game/script.rpy	317	l "[what]"
start_9eff490b		He snaps his fingers again and Emrys falls from his web. A procession of spiders softens his fall and parades him out of the classroom.	game/script.rpy	322	"[what]"
start_90bcff48	l	Don’t worry, they’ll deliver him safely back to where he came from.	game/script.rpy	323	l "[what]"
start_77a18e15	l	Now, we have work to do, my dearest partner!	game/script.rpy	325	l "[what]"
start_e231dc2a	e	What on Earth was that all about?!	game/script.rpy	335	e "[what]"
start_f9799323	l	Hmm, what do you mean?	game/script.rpy	338	l "[what]"
start_fa17289f	e	That was my first kiss! You don’t just get to take it!	game/script.rpy	339	e "[what]"
start_21d43b64	l	Oh, that? I mean, we could’ve intermingled our blood if you preferred. I thought this would be most agreeable to human sensibilities.	game/script.rpy	342	l "[what]"
start_430c59f8	l	Was I wrong?	game/script.rpy	343	l "[what]"
start_72a33094	e	...	game/script.rpy	347	e "[what]"
start_72a33094_1	e	...	game/script.rpy	351	e "[what]"
start_4b7b2ae6	e	Hmph! If that really was the only way then I guess there’s no helping it!	game/script.rpy	352	e "[what]"
start_e6f960cc	l	But I just said it wasn’t the only way?	game/script.rpy	355	l "[what]"
start_e55f3af9	e	Argh!	game/script.rpy	359	e "[what]"
start_aa80cf93		The setting sun coats the abandoned classroom in a pleasant, warm glow.	game/script.rpy	366	"[what]"
start_fbb55aca		The air is dense with specks of dust that twirl and dance, illuminated by the sun’s rays.	game/script.rpy	367	"[what]"
start_95fa4c31		Desks and chairs are stacked haphazardly against the south wall, holding forgotten belongings never to be retrieved again.	game/script.rpy	368	"[what]"
start_ea1ec8be		Only the astute eye would notice an unnatural amount of spiders hiding in various nooks and crannies, marking the territory of their prince.	game/script.rpy	369	"[what]"
start_13e53eaf	l	Well, it’s about time for me to give you your first task!	game/script.rpy	373	l "[what]"
start_148006fa	l	Before we can get to work, we’re going to need a suitable base of operations...	game/script.rpy	377	l "[what]"
start_3df93235	e	What do you even need a human for anyway?	game/script.rpy	378	e evening "[what]"
start_d80b567f	l	All in due time, my dearest partner.	game/script.rpy	382	l "[what]"
start_fe4d60e3	l	First, this place needs to be set in order! My classroom should not be this decrepit.	game/script.rpy	386	l "[what]"
start_b65e2a25	e	Is an abandoned classroom really the best you can do for a hideout?	game/script.rpy	390	e "[what]"
start_770a63a0		His face inches towards mine. A chill runs up my spine.	game/script.rpy	394	"[what]"
start_25cf693e		I let my guard down. He’s dangerous—I can't forget that.	game/script.rpy	395	"[what]"
start_c292f627		The way his face can change from charming to terrifying at the drop of a hat... I can’t decide if I’m impressed or disturbed.	game/script.rpy	396	"[what]"
start_cf91e0e4	l	Do you not trust my judgment?	game/script.rpy	397	l "[what]"
start_ea902478		He turns on his heels and paces the room as he continues.	game/script.rpy	401	"[what]"
start_2c1a20d9	l	The boundary is thinnest in this exact location. If an apparition wants to cross over into this world, they’re likely to pass through this classroom.	game/script.rpy	404	l "[what]"
start_f1fd8dda	l	Not to mention I can tap into my powers more easily without crossing over.	game/script.rpy	407	l "[what]"
start_b10fa492		I listen to his explanation as I follow his instructions to tidy up the room, gathering up the belongings of students who have long since graduated.	game/script.rpy	408	"[what]"
start_1b8ff781		Lucifrid smiles and pats my head. Well, tries to, as I push one of his four hands away.	game/script.rpy	413	"[what]"
start_36a13cc7	l	You’re surprisingly obedient, aren’t you?	game/script.rpy	414	l "[what]"
start_300f8729	e	Hmph, I just have a sense of responsibility.	game/script.rpy	418	e "[what]"
start_72a33094_2	e	...	game/script.rpy	419	e "[what]"
start_3cf08955	e	But you're right! Why am I doing this? You have more hands than I do!	game/script.rpy	423	e "[what]"
start_75b752cd	e	And you’re a fiend who threatened my assistant, forced me into this arrangement and {i}stole my first kiss!{/i}	game/script.rpy	427	e "[what]"
start_de39fa53	l	Hmmm~ You’re cute even when you’re angry.	game/script.rpy	431	l "[what]"
start_a80a64ec	l	Did the kiss bother you that much?	game/script.rpy	432	l "[what]"
start_cf3bd943	l	My~ soul~ mate~	game/script.rpy	436	l "[what]"
start_5ee7c575		What kind of apparition is he...	game/script.rpy	437	"[what]"
start_68e531b4		Why did I have to get caught up in this...	game/script.rpy	438	"[what]"
start_ab7ed8e0		Emrys better be real grateful.	game/script.rpy	439	"[what]"
start_7dd08f50		The sun sinks further and further as I thoroughly clean the dusty classroom.	game/script.rpy	443	"[what]"
start_90b4a1ea		In the meantime, Lucifrid lounges around while playing with his familiars.	game/script.rpy	444	"[what]"
start_64dbf3ce		They still give me the creeps...	game/script.rpy	445	"[what]"
start_55960a4e	e	Why don’t you help out a little?! Or at least ask your little followers to help me out!	game/script.rpy	449	e "[what]"
start_f56230d8		He turns around languidly and the very movement annoys me.	game/script.rpy	450	"[what]"
start_1ee17702		Here I am, toiling away my beautiful summer afternoon—time I could have been spending so many better ways—and he can’t even appreciate it!	game/script.rpy	451	"[what]"
start_6f3a9fb2		After a long pause he opens his mouth.	game/script.rpy	452	"[what]"
start_f163ce69	l	Hmm...	game/script.rpy	456	l "[what]"
start_c3312325	l	Let me think...	game/script.rpy	457	l "[what]"
start_80818862	e	Answer me properly!	game/script.rpy	458	e "[what]"
start_2ba40322	l	Alright, I won’t help then, hehe!	game/script.rpy	462	l "[what]"
start_7ddea6bb		He turns back around and continues his game with the spiders.	game/script.rpy	466	"[what]"
start_a20cefa7		...	game/script.rpy	467	"[what]"
start_7a90d61a		A deep sigh escapes me.	game/script.rpy	468	"[what]"
start_0e42c71a		By the time everything is sorted out and set up, the day has firmly turned into night and I'm pretty sure we’re the only ones left in the school building.	game/script.rpy	469	"[what]"
start_6d5ba2d7	e	Well Your Majesty, please take to your throne.	game/script.rpy	473	e "[what]"
start_95bc8076		I gesture to the paint-peeled chair beside the desk, arranged meticulously according to Lucifrid’s vision, but his prideful smirk doesn’t falter.	game/script.rpy	474	"[what]"
start_2227695f		Something tells me he isn’t taking my sarcasm the way I intended it.	game/script.rpy	475	"[what]"
start_b82316b1	l	Well done, my assistant. I think this deserves a little reward.	game/script.rpy	479	l "[what]"
start_58324ada		My suspicious expression remains undisturbed.	game/script.rpy	480	"[what]"
start_895a5da4		One of the little spiders runs up to me carrying a piece of candy on its back.	game/script.rpy	481	"[what]"
start_5b47c350		I try my hardest to keep frowning but fine, it’s kind of cute.	game/script.rpy	482	"[what]"
start_473b3375		I seat myself atop one of the desks as I unwrap the spider’s treat and pop it into my mouth.	game/script.rpy	483	"[what]"
start_b84e49ca		It’s sour and sweet, melting easily on my tongue.	game/script.rpy	484	"[what]"
start_ae943d01		Not nearly equivalent to all my hard work, but I'll take it.	game/script.rpy	485	"[what]"
start_66312e4d	e	So, can you tell me your master plan yet?	game/script.rpy	489	e "[what]"
start_8175d530	l	Edelweiss of Hesgothia. I’ve been sensing your power since you entered this school.	game/script.rpy	493	l "[what]"
start_f1844953	l	Your blood has a strong affinity with the spirit realm, but have you ever been across the boundary?	game/script.rpy	494	l "[what]"
start_0f2c7c91	e	H-heh, what kind of top class diviner would I be if I hadn’t even set foot in the spirit realm myself?	game/script.rpy	498	e "[what]"
start_3f2fd57d_1	l	Hmmmm, is that so?	game/script.rpy	502	l "[what]"
start_22b82c21		He gently twirls a strand of my hair around his finger as his eyes seem to pierce straight through to my core.	game/script.rpy	503	"[what]"
start_52a2f14d	l	{i}Ehehehe!{/i}	game/script.rpy	507	l "[what]"
start_b52b01cd	l	It’s no good to lie to your trusted partner.	game/script.rpy	511	l "[what]"
start_79914aa1		Heat rises to my cheeks. How does he know I was bluffing...?	game/script.rpy	512	"[what]"
start_80699b40	l	If you don’t properly anchor yourself you won’t be able to return, you know!	game/script.rpy	516	l "[what]"
start_8af26edf	l	But you are bound to me, so I’m all you need.	game/script.rpy	520	l "[what]"
start_7dc65aeb	l	You’ll be seeing a lot of the beyond soon.	game/script.rpy	524	l "[what]"
start_77ffed7a	l	But fine, let me show you exactly where you fit into my plans...	game/script.rpy	528	l "[what]"
start_fd14a798		He claps one pair of hands, and sinks the other two into the desk arrangement, seemingly phasing them out of existence.	game/script.rpy	531	"[what]"
start_b9022503		Is he... reaching into the beyond? Interesting.	game/script.rpy	532	"[what]"
start_759d71a8		Bit by bit I'm realising exactly how much I don't know about apparitions.	game/script.rpy	536	"[what]"
start_db835756		If my mother were here, would she have been able to handle this situation better? Would she have bested Lucifrid the moment they met?	game/script.rpy	537	"[what]"
start_8952659a		If my mother were here... I could have at least asked for her advice.	game/script.rpy	538	"[what]"
start_a60bf457		Her figure surfaces in my mind, but she’s faint and I can’t quite make out her face. It’s been a long time after all.	game/script.rpy	539	"[what]"
start_cc228a99		Would she scold me? If father knew I had somehow gotten myself into a contract with an apparition deity he would be furious...	game/script.rpy	540	"[what]"
start_a8e48ea1		But I have a feeling she would’ve responded differently.	game/script.rpy	541	"[what]"
start_d4ab5ec3	"Mother"	Oh Edie, reckless as always.	game/script.rpy	542	"Mother" "[what]"
start_5e752a6f		The mother in my imagination laughs softly, her voice clear as day.	game/script.rpy	543	"[what]"
start_138e56f7	"Mother"	You’ve made your own mess—now it's your duty to get yourself out of it. Rise to the challenge. It can only help you grow.	game/script.rpy	544	"Mother" "[what]"
start_e2999ee5		The encouragement doesn’t ring as hollow as expected. Is she... really there?	game/script.rpy	545	"[what]"
start_c1c4b7f0		But that would be impossible.	game/script.rpy	546	"[what]"
start_ad759dd5		I snap out of my reverie with a start.	game/script.rpy	549	"[what]"
start_2da6a3cc	l	Edelweiss... pay attention. This part is important.	game/script.rpy	552	l "[what]"
start_54b4308a	l	Here. This is my tome. Everything contained in it is mine to control.	game/script.rpy	555	l "[what]"
start_eba73bd4		He rifles through the pages, stopping upon a page filled with red ink that seems like it has barely dried.	game/script.rpy	558	"[what]"
start_b4c8fa06		I can’t make out any of the characters until he slowly drags his finger over the words.	game/script.rpy	559	"[what]"
start_fa9c55af	e	Ah! It’s my name.	game/script.rpy	563	e "[what]"
start_b57f9aab	l	Yes, it is proof that we are bound together.	game/script.rpy	567	l "[what]"
start_bb353136	l	Names hold a high authority in the spirit realm, but only humans can truly claim the names of apparitions.	game/script.rpy	571	l "[what]"
start_ad8692d0	l	Apparitions are like smoke, their names can make them corporeal, but only if there is something corporeal to tie them down. Do you follow?	game/script.rpy	575	l "[what]"
start_55013b0a	e	Somewhat... I think...	game/script.rpy	579	e "[what]"
start_8f1a906f		My lessons covered something like this once, but I can’t quite recall the details.	game/script.rpy	580	"[what]"
start_ce424968		A lot of my family’s knowledge is passed down for generations through nothing but scrawled notes and incomplete observations.	game/script.rpy	581	"[what]"
start_56762ab5		Father is from a minor branch family and mostly minds the affairs at home, so when mother passed away young, she took a lot of information with her to the grave.	game/script.rpy	582	"[what]"
start_00442f1e	l	Well, it matters not. What matters is that you will claim the names of all my opponents for me, so that I may reign over the dark side of this school undisputedly.	game/script.rpy	586	l "[what]"
start_8871293d	l	Don’t worry, I’ll let you reign alongside me, that’s only fair.	game/script.rpy	590	l "[what]"
start_cc5b49b7		He laughs, unconcerned with whether I {i}want{/i} to reign alongside him.	game/script.rpy	591	"[what]"
start_7cee395d	e	Your... opponents? You have many of those?	game/script.rpy	595	e "[what]"
start_fe49bf20	l	Oh, apparitions rarely play nice if someone’s encroaching on their territory.	game/script.rpy	599	l "[what]"
start_6ceaa032	l	There’s many who don’t even have capability for reason, though most are of the 'live and let live' mentality.	game/script.rpy	603	l "[what]"
start_1583d51c	l	Though I personally do not intend to let live, {i}ehe.{/i}	game/script.rpy	607	l "[what]"
start_087edfb6	e	So you’re looking to stage a bloody revolution? I’ve become the assistant to an evil oppressor?!	game/script.rpy	611	e "[what]"
start_389641a4		Well, I can hardly say I'm surprised. A noble creature would not have threatened to murder my friend in order to get me to help with his plans.	game/script.rpy	612	"[what]"
start_b4d279d3		It's just another conflict between apparitions. I can't feel too guilty over whatever I do under coercion, and it's not like they'd care if there were humans in their path...	game/script.rpy	613	"[what]"
start_17a268be		I just have to play along for now. There has to be some way out of this.	game/script.rpy	614	"[what]"
start_e7a4f6a4	l	Oh, don’t be like that! They’re a disorganised mess right now! I’m doing them a favour by giving them a purpose.	game/script.rpy	618	l "[what]"
start_12a13c5b	l	A unified spirit realm will be for the benefit of everyone.	game/script.rpy	622	l "[what]"
start_5f30ffb8	e	Everyone except humans...	game/script.rpy	624	e "[what]"
start_860b49e9		He responds with nothing but a wide, almost innocent smile. Guess that’s my answer.	game/script.rpy	625	"[what]"
start_de19face		Well, let's not stir the pot. If I can earn his trust, maybe I can catch him off guard.	game/script.rpy	626	"[what]"
start_3c1a628b	e	I’ll take it as a learning experience for my future as a diviner!	game/script.rpy	628	e "[what]"
start_0d5c068e		There’s nothing to do but look on the bright side and make the best of it.	game/script.rpy	629	"[what]"
start_a931c144		Or at the very least, convince Lucifrid that that's what I'm doing.	game/script.rpy	630	"[what]"
start_3f0e56cb	l	Mm, mm!	game/script.rpy	632	l "[what]"
start_a02e12dd		He nods emphatically.	game/script.rpy	633	"[what]"
start_d15bd8b4	l	I’m glad we were able to see eye to eye!	game/script.rpy	634	l "[what]"
start_97e01170	e	I wouldn’t quite put it that way...	game/script.rpy	636	e "[what]"
start_47e9dc57	l	I’ll see you here tomorrow after class! For now you’re dismissed!	game/script.rpy	638	l "[what]"
start_e36ca779	em	Alright, I'll give you the keyword and you tell me what you know.	game/script.rpy	647	em "[what]"
start_4a6f6de7	e	Mm-hm.	game/script.rpy	649	e "[what]"
start_3f73206b	em	{i}Diviner.{/i}	game/script.rpy	650	em "[what]"
start_76b11543	e	What? Is this really necessary? Of course I know that!	game/script.rpy	652	e "[what]"
start_5644a977	em	The basics are the basics for a reason.	game/script.rpy	654	em "[what]"
start_d60f6444	e	Individuals from a bloodline with a strong connection to the beyond. They can see apparitions and exercise some power over them.	game/script.rpy	656	e "[what]"
start_a24bcfca	em	That's too broad.	game/script.rpy	657	em "[what]"
start_12b68a10	e	I wasn't done yet! They keep balance between the human realm and the spirit realm and try to seek peaceful solutions, like sealing an apparition instead of banishing it.	game/script.rpy	661	e "[what]"
start_f07e160e	em	Alright, what about exorcists?	game/script.rpy	665	em "[what]"
start_e3945d83	e	Similar powers, different approach. They usually possess stronger tools and rituals to dispose of apparitions. They're uh, fight before flight.	game/script.rpy	669	e "[what]"
start_ee5611c0		Emrys opens his mouth, probably to reprimand my casual speech, but closes it again and just nods.	game/script.rpy	673	"[what]"
start_b7ca465c	em	Next, the beyond.	game/script.rpy	674	em "[what]"
start_e13d4523	e	It's where apparitions live. It's like, another layer of this world.	game/script.rpy	675	e "[what]"
start_e2272f88	em	I don't think your father will be satisfied with that answer.	game/script.rpy	679	em "[what]"
start_e8425279	e	Well, it's vague! Nobody can agree on exactly what it is! Sometimes it's just the same as our world, and sometimes it's completely different.	game/script.rpy	683	e "[what]"
start_5e127f37	em	It's connected to our world, and overlaps in places, but not everywhere. It's oversimplifying to call it another layer.	game/script.rpy	687	em "[what]"
start_148fdc5c	e	Fiiiine.	game/script.rpy	691	e "[what]"
start_c7b64bf0	em	Next. The boundary.	game/script.rpy	692	em "[what]"
start_5295e744	e	The dividing line between our world and the beyond. Crossing over is possible, but requires rituals, and it's quite dangerous.	game/script.rpy	696	e "[what]"
start_a4a6b3cb	e	The work of a diviner usually starts when apparitions cross the boundary. Sometimes humans summon them, purposefully or inadvertently. But some of them can cross over on their own.	game/script.rpy	697	e "[what]"
start_1ac59604	em	That's more like it.	game/script.rpy	700	em "[what]"
start_9dda4dae	e	You really think my dad's gonna ask things like this?	game/script.rpy	703	e "[what]"
start_6bc7baab	em	He's trying to be serious about your education. Conducting exams is part of that.	game/script.rpy	705	em "[what]"
start_af9dd0ec	em	You'll do fine. Maybe he'll finally let you carry one of your mom's talismans after this.	game/script.rpy	707	em "[what]"
start_f53f21cc	e	As if. I wish he'd take me seriously... How am I supposed to learn without any hands-on experience?	game/script.rpy	709	e "[what]"
start_9ec4c406		True to his word, Lucifrid has made sure Emrys remembers nothing of his spidery ordeal. He's back to quizzing me on theory like nothing happened.	game/script.rpy	710	"[what]"
start_f7579cc7		I suppose I'll be getting plenty of hands-on experience soon enough...	game/script.rpy	711	"[what]"
start_62ceb17c	em	I'll put in a good word for you if you do well on the exam, maybe he'll listen to me.	game/script.rpy	712	em "[what]"
start_c0351306	e	Can't believe my own father trusts you more than me but yeah, that might actually help.	game/script.rpy	714	e "[what]"
start_c070acdf	em	So with that, wanna hang out at the arcade?	game/script.rpy	717	em "[what]"
start_a0c61235	e	Ah, um, I can’t, I’ve got... stuff.	game/script.rpy	720	e "[what]"
start_5dd43710		It would be foolish to give up the one advantage I’ve gained by teaming up with Lucifrid, but my mind is drawing a blank on a convincing excuse.	game/script.rpy	721	"[what]"
start_c206b7d5	em	What, don’t tell me you’ve started taking your schoolwork seriously! If it's more diviner business I'll help out.	game/script.rpy	723	em "[what]"
start_9fac4a8e	e	Schoolwork!{nw=1.5}	game/script.rpy	725	e "[what]"
start_5112e363	extend e	 Yes, that’s what it is! You know, with test week coming up and all...	game/script.rpy	727	extend "[what]"
start_af9e0a50	em	...	game/script.rpy	730	em "[what]"
start_8307b0bd		A man couldn’t look more incredulous if he tried. Guess Emrys knows me better than that.	game/script.rpy	731	"[what]"
start_e551cb3a	e	Ahaha, you got me!	game/script.rpy	734	e "[what]"
start_ca9ad049	e	Maybe it wouldn’t be a bad idea to blow off steam at the arcade.	game/script.rpy	736	e "[what]"
start_5579d1da	em	I thought losing made your mood worse, not better.	game/script.rpy	738	em "[what]"
start_31a51ef6	e	It does. I was more thinking of watching you lose, personally.	game/script.rpy	742	e "[what]"
start_925ad694		I mean, Lucifrid {i}did{/i} tell me to meet him after class today but it’s not like I explicitly agreed to it or anything...	game/script.rpy	743	"[what]"
start_d967175c		Besides, apparitions operate within their own domains. If I just make it out of the school there should be nothing he can do.	game/script.rpy	744	"[what]"
start_108e2a65		That settles it.	game/script.rpy	745	"[what]"
start_89a92ef5	e	Fine, you’re right, I don’t need to do the stuff today.	game/script.rpy	749	e "[what]"
start_eb825565	em	Whatever your "stuff" is, it better not be dangerous.	game/script.rpy	751	em "[what]"
start_40eea6a8		I’d say he’s being overprotective, but I can't exactly argue that meddling in apparition domain wars {i}isn't{/i} dangerous.	game/script.rpy	752	"[what]"
start_61077df5		Well, better make something up.	game/script.rpy	753	"[what]"
start_ab6fee92	e	Oh no, of course not! Just, you know, girl things.	game/script.rpy	754	e "[what]"
start_a18b1089		Like hanging out with spider apparitions. As all girls do.	game/script.rpy	755	"[what]"
start_f39c9dfb		We make our way down to the first floor and Emrys takes a last minute bathroom break. Tension builds up inside me.	game/script.rpy	763	"[what]"
start_c32dbedb		This is so not the time! We have to get out of here!	game/script.rpy	764	"[what]"
start_19665ea0		...Is what I’d like to say, but I have to play it cool. Instead I wait patiently by the front entrance.	game/script.rpy	765	"[what]"
start_b3ad4871	l	What exactly do you think you’re doing?	game/script.rpy	770	l "[what]"
start_a0c4491d	l	Foolish human. We are quite literally bound to each other’s life essence and you thought you could sneak out unnoticed?	game/script.rpy	771	l "[what]"
start_58262e26		Though Lucifrid is barely an inch taller than me, right now his presence is looming.	game/script.rpy	772	"[what]"
start_d2ce5bcb		The atmosphere of the entire hallway darkens as my pulse speeds up.	game/script.rpy	773	"[what]"
start_d84fdec5		I can’t do much but stare and stammer. I have no excuse.	game/script.rpy	774	"[what]"
start_692f8bf4		I {i}did{/i} think I could sneak out unnoticed.	game/script.rpy	775	"[what]"
start_2f31112f	l	But no matter! I’ll discipline you one way or another. Though I was so looking forward to our burgeoning camaraderie, hehe.	game/script.rpy	779	l "[what]"
start_97d90951	e	I-I’m sorry! I just didn’t know what to—	game/script.rpy	783	e "[what]"
start_4dff4cf3		Two of his hands clamp over my mouth, the other two spin me around. Emrys is walking over.	game/script.rpy	787	"[what]"
start_c12aa1d6	l	Hush now, you wouldn’t want him to get suspicious.	game/script.rpy	788	l "[what]"
start_a89fbe68		I try to calm my breathing and pretend I’m not deeply terrified.	game/script.rpy	789	"[what]"
start_f18b26cb	em	Edelweiss, your face is pale, is everything alright?{nw=1.0} 	game/script.rpy	794	em "[what]"
start_1ababcdb	extend em	{size=-8}...Apparitions again?{/size}	game/script.rpy	795	extend "[what]"
start_7d46cc7a		He whispers it as he leans in, completely unaware of the third party in our little gathering.	game/script.rpy	796	"[what]"
start_307cb107		I didn’t know Lucifrid could erase his presence like that, but I guess Emrys’ spiritual abilities are easily thrown off—he can't see him.	game/script.rpy	797	"[what]"
start_e7185385	e	Oh yeah, a real scary-looking spider just crawled past. Probably harmless though!	game/script.rpy	801	e "[what]"
start_f11dad7b	e	Listen, I got a call and it looks like my plans really can’t wait. I’m sorry for being all wishy-washy. I’ll make it up to you some other time, I promise.	game/script.rpy	805	e "[what]"
start_93fc4d33		Lucifrid’s eyes narrow.	game/script.rpy	809	"[what]"
start_8f6ef413	e	O-on the weekends, you know. When I have more time!	game/script.rpy	813	e "[what]"
start_1d65aa65	l	This won't do. Say something to throw him off.	game/script.rpy	815	l "[what]"
start_7721d05f		Well, I know one thing I can say to stop Emrys from digging further. But that's no longer little white lie territory, that's big black lie. And I'm not sure I feel good about it.	game/script.rpy	816	"[what]"
start_9eee6e4b		I look over at Lucifrid nervously, but his menacing glower has lost none of its intensity.	game/script.rpy	817	"[what]"
start_411e2a61		I swallow hard.	game/script.rpy	818	"[what]"
start_4fa60668	em	Hey, don’t forget I’m not {i}just{/i} your assistant. I want to spend time with you off-duty all the same.	game/script.rpy	821	em "[what]"
start_23e030f7	e	I know that. I’m happy about that.	game/script.rpy	825	e "[what]"
start_9fe4add1		Forgive me Emrys. This is all to protect you.	game/script.rpy	826	"[what]"
start_dc8696a0	e	I would never forget my best friend just because I got a boyfriend.	game/script.rpy	827	e "[what]"
start_1687457e		Emrys blushes. Lucifrid grins.	game/script.rpy	832	"[what]"
start_7dc443b3	em	A boyfriend...? When did you find the time to{cps=3}...{/cps} Is he taking good care of you at least?	game/script.rpy	833	em "[what]"
start_20094d45	l	I didn't know you thought of me that way, Edie.	game/script.rpy	837	l "[what]"
start_fc224b29		Lucifrid languidly slings two arms around me as I try my best to keep my composure.	game/script.rpy	838	"[what]"
start_dd1160db		I’m going to regret this, aren’t I?	game/script.rpy	839	"[what]"
start_661b7565	e	I’ll tell you the details sometime, once I know for sure it’s the real thing.	game/script.rpy	843	e "[what]"
start_75c230df	e	Just go on ahead, Emrys! I’ll see you in class tomorrow.	game/script.rpy	847	e "[what]"
start_1affe1e9		Emrys dips his head, bashful. As I look at his face, the shame of deceit washes over me.	game/script.rpy	848	"[what]"
start_a743663f		I watch his frame move into the distance and promise myself I’ll tell him the truth eventually. He’ll understand.{w} He'll understand, right?	game/script.rpy	853	"[what]"
start_9808fc68		...He'll definitely tell father. I don't even want to imagine the scolding I’ll receive.	game/script.rpy	854	"[what]"
start_16624580		But what's done is done. Regret can wait.	game/script.rpy	855	"[what]"
start_63a5b3d2		Lucifrid pushes me towards the staircase and I stumble unceremoniously.	game/script.rpy	859	"[what]"
start_49a63583	l	Onward, underling. We’ve wasted enough time.	game/script.rpy	860	l "[what]"
start_8ddf3778	l	Are we clear on the plan?	game/script.rpy	870	l "[what]"
start_b8ea3756	e	I follow your lead and stay behind you until you’ve subdued the enemy, at which point I’ll open the tome and say: ‘Speak thy name and thine allegiance be manifest.’	game/script.rpy	871	e "[what]"
start_18af48ce		He hums contentedly.	game/script.rpy	875	"[what]"
start_35395560	l	Seems like we’re ready.	game/script.rpy	879	l "[what]"
start_2837edaa	l	Now, take my hand. Don’t be afraid.	game/script.rpy	883	l "[what]"
start_cf65bf4c		I try to steady my breathing as I link our hands, forming an anchor for safe passage across the boundary. I'm not afraid. I'm not afraid.	game/script.rpy	884	"[what]"
start_ed961259		The hands-on experience father wouldn't allow me... is coming sooner than I expected.	game/script.rpy	885	"[what]"
start_a0621e7b	e	Wait!	game/script.rpy	889	e "[what]"
start_579ab600	l	Hmm?	game/script.rpy	893	l "[what]"
start_471e5147	e	Can I whack them over the head with the tome while I chant?	game/script.rpy	897	e "[what]"
start_afa997f1		Lucifrid bursts out laughing.	game/script.rpy	901	"[what]"
start_f701ae03	l	Well, I don't see why not.	game/script.rpy	902	l "[what]"
start_85881070		The air contorts. I squeeze my eyes shut, feeling briefly like I might lose consciousness.	game/script.rpy	906	"[what]"
start_1de3f3cf		All sense perception leaves me save a hazy weightlessness and the feeling of Lucifrid's hand in mine. For a brief moment I am nowhere and everywhere.	game/script.rpy	907	"[what]"
start_b61785ce		My feet land on solid ground. I open my eyes.	game/script.rpy	914	"[what]"
start_c6968003		There stands the prince of spiders with his battalion of familiars, cast in a dim, eerie light. The classroom around us appears... normal.	game/script.rpy	915	"[what]"
start_58c802fa		Upon closer inspection, eyes peer out from places they shouldn’t, and everything sways and twists—as though the edges between objects are not quite laws, but more like suggestions of physics.	game/script.rpy	916	"[what]"
start_6b38784b		A piercing wind shrieks and howls in a way it should not be able to inside a school building, chilling me to my core.	game/script.rpy	919	"[what]"
start_a7113256		I’m suddenly glad for the faint warmth of Lucifrid’s hand in mine.	game/script.rpy	920	"[what]"
start_7fd0a075		He looks me over and nods as he steps forward, defying the fierce headwind opposing us.	game/script.rpy	921	"[what]"
start_89ed2fd1		So we walk. Onward and onward. And onward.{w} And onward.	game/script.rpy	922	"[what]"
start_48f67590		A distance that should have taken us minutes, if not seconds to cross stretches endlessly, as the blackboard at the front of the classroom remains ever distant.	game/script.rpy	923	"[what]"
start_a68b6286	l	Come out, come out, wherever you are!	game/script.rpy	927	l "[what]"
start_272682b0		In the blink of an eye, Lucifrid shoots silky threads in four directions, coating the room in pathways for his familiars.	game/script.rpy	928	"[what]"
start_c5cc9133		The spider battalion spreads out in formation, scoping out the denizen of this mysterious place.	game/script.rpy	929	"[what]"
start_4dd52a50	e	Who... or what are we even looking for?	game/script.rpy	930	e beyond "[what]"
start_27224808		I lean forward, trying to peer past the desks ahead of us.	game/script.rpy	931	"[what]"
start_7f3d9aad	l	Stay back, Edelweiss. These threads are sharper than they look.	game/script.rpy	935	l "[what]"
start_1e5e4507		I jolt back. The room is so cold that even the light glinting off Lucifrid’s web seems like it could freeze.	game/script.rpy	936	"[what]"
start_eafe562b		He clenches a fist. The web around the teacher’s desk coils and cinches, slicing through solid wood with ease.	game/script.rpy	937	"[what]"
start_595d2ebc	l	Heh, I think someone didn’t like that.	game/script.rpy	943	l "[what]"
start_8a4cc2e9		The breeze howls into a gale. As Lucifrid's web spans more and more of the classroom, frost crystallises on every thread.	game/script.rpy	947	"[what]"
start_08b787de		A glacial maelstrom gathers itself into a ghastly cloaked figure. Its long hair billows, obscuring its features as it wheezes at us.	game/script.rpy	953	"[what]"
start_26bffc1a	"Ghost"	Leave this place.	game/script.rpy	954	"Ghost" "[what]"
start_e9fadab7	l	Terribly afraid I can’t do that.	game/script.rpy	959	l "[what]"
start_20f9a6f3		Lucifrid’s familiars have begun clambering up the creature’s robes.	game/script.rpy	960	"[what]"
start_04e44e78		Right as I feel a tinge of pity for it, it dashes forward,	game/script.rpy	962	"[what]"
start_84d2ebdb	extend 	 scattering the arachnid battalion off its vestments and shooting icicles in our direction.	game/script.rpy	964	extend "[what]"
start_eb5090a0	"Ghost"	Stay away...	game/script.rpy	965	"Ghost" "[what]"
start_c7838793		Lucifrid avoids the attack nimbly, stopping one of the projectiles just short of hitting me in the process.	game/script.rpy	966	"[what]"
start_8d173bf9		No time to feel sorry now.	game/script.rpy	967	"[what]"
start_25208c60	l	Take cover and bide your time.	game/script.rpy	971	l "[what]"
start_b076a398		I follow his instructions and hide behind a student’s desk, watching as he continues to taunt the snow spirit.	game/script.rpy	972	"[what]"
start_81f854d4		It seems to lose its temper the longer it fails to hit a single strike.	game/script.rpy	973	"[what]"
start_4b24ac5d	l	Hehehe, haha! Is that all you've got?	game/script.rpy	977	l "[what]"
start_a5de9a73		It rushes forward too desperately and carelessly gets tangled in the spider prince’s web. It's helplessly trapped.	game/script.rpy	978	"[what]"
start_02aa7e4c		Lucifrid toyingly flexes his fingers, the web cutting and slicing with his every move.	game/script.rpy	979	"[what]"
start_e3c932eb	"Ghost"	Uuuh...	game/script.rpy	982	"Ghost" "[what]"
start_b119aff6		Isn’t he being too cruel? Our opponent is defenseless!	game/script.rpy	983	"[what]"
start_4e70fb8a	e	Did no one ever teach you not to play with your food?	game/script.rpy	987	e "[what]"
start_48b8e833	l	Ah, a classic human saying, isn't it? But where do you think we are?	game/script.rpy	988	l "[what]"
start_d8eff16a	l	I can even express it in your terms. I believe it goes... "when in Rome"?	game/script.rpy	990	l "[what]"
start_2ad4e542		That smug little...	game/script.rpy	991	"[what]"
start_82d4a259		Instead of waiting for a signal, I cut his playtime short and run ahead with the tome in tow.	game/script.rpy	996	"[what]"
start_66948882	e2	State thy name and thine allegiance be manifest!	game/script.rpy	997	e2 "[what]"
start_923ad509		I smash the creature with all the strength I can muster. I don't even hear the syllables it spits out over the sound of the blood rushing to my head.	game/script.rpy	999	"[what]"
start_73d63856		Ink flows across the tome’s opened pages and the creature slinks away. Immediately the air calms and warmth returns to the room.	game/script.rpy	1000	"[what]"
start_a240352e		The breath I didn't know I was holding in slips out with a sigh.	game/script.rpy	1001	"[what]"
start_24a44cbd		Lucifrid dissolves his webs with a swift exhale, his expression displeased.	game/script.rpy	1005	"[what]"
start_f8614294	l	You’re not too good at taking orders, are you? My cumbersome partner.	game/script.rpy	1010	l "[what]"
start_d084cb2b	e	Partner implies a relationship between equals. I can act on my own authority!	game/script.rpy	1014	e "[what]"
start_9c0f0ddc	e	I got the job done, didn’t I? Who knows, maybe that thing would have broken free from your web in no time!	game/script.rpy	1015	e "[what]"
start_04040d92	l	Hah, not a chance.	game/script.rpy	1019	l "[what]"
start_838816d7	l	I wanted to bully that one a little longer! Guess I’ll have to content myself with bullying you.	game/script.rpy	1023	l "[what]"
start_988af4b4		He pinches my cheek just hard enough that it hurts—but I refuse to give him the satisfaction of acknowledging the pain.	game/script.rpy	1024	"[what]"
start_2bc6be2f	e	Hmph. Be careful or I'll teach you another saying. You reap what you sow.	game/script.rpy	1028	e "[what]"
start_277c1bb6	l	Hmm, not sure that one's relevant to me. {i}Hehe.{/i}	game/script.rpy	1032	l "[what]"
start_e19c1e0f		I shake my head and move on.	game/script.rpy	1033	"[what]"
start_14740a06	e	...So, what happens to that apparition now?	game/script.rpy	1037	e "[what]"
start_9c86fbfa	l	It's entirely mine! Powerless until I say the word, its territory incorporated into my domain effective immediately.	game/script.rpy	1041	l "[what]"
start_52c5806f	e	So is this classroom free of outside influence on the other side of the boundary too?	game/script.rpy	1042	e "[what]"
start_37a470c0	l	Mhm-mhm! Light side or dark side, it's mine. Though alas, my power is still limited in the human realm.	game/script.rpy	1043	l "[what]"
start_bbb632a1	e	And that ice spirit is just... gone until you call upon it?	game/script.rpy	1044	e "[what]"
start_b184db9b	l	Familiars are free to wander around as they please! They can't do any harm anyway.{nw=1.5}	game/script.rpy	1045	l "[what]"
start_05bdc1c2	extend l	 Endlessly benevolent, aren't I?	game/script.rpy	1047	extend "[what]"
start_66ad86e5		It’s... less cruel than I expected, though I suppose pragmatism is the ruling principle here.	game/script.rpy	1048	"[what]"
start_ba9b9a31		It leaves me to wonder what a cruel fate for an apparition would even look like.	game/script.rpy	1049	"[what]"
start_80b9e4bf	e	How do apparitions even die? Do apparitions die?	game/script.rpy	1050	e "[what]"
start_dbfbd444	l	Hmm, it’s more like they wax and wane... they don’t truly disappear like humans do. Though an eternal waning is pretty much the same as death.	game/script.rpy	1054	l "[what]"
start_7f965b37	l	As long as someone remembers us and calls upon us, we can return.	game/script.rpy	1055	l "[what]"
start_83529d5d	e	I guess being forgotten is the final end for humans and spirits alike.	game/script.rpy	1059	e "[what]"
start_608b2591	l	Well, that’s through natural means. You pesky humans have devised ways to exorcise us. You’re far more cruel than us!	game/script.rpy	1063	l "[what]"
start_0730793b	e	There’s apparitions that threaten to destroy entire communities! Sometimes harsh measures are justified.	game/script.rpy	1067	e "[what]"
start_c76a59a1	l	Mm, mm. Glad you’re starting to warm to my point of view.	game/script.rpy	1071	l "[what]"
start_f5d80162		Purposefully twisting my words again, huh? Now it’s my turn to pinch his cheek.	game/script.rpy	1072	"[what]"
start_93bb2c23		...Squishy.	game/script.rpy	1073	"[what]"
start_3688cade	l	Hey, ow! That hurts!	game/script.rpy	1077	l "[what]"
start_7e88197a	e	Merely returning the favour. After sowing comes reaping, I warned you.	game/script.rpy	1081	e "[what]"
start_d8d5a170	l	...These crops are growing unreasonably quickly.	game/script.rpy	1082	l "[what]"
start_60b9e14f	l	Now off you go, your duty is done. I've had quite enough of you.	game/script.rpy	1083	l "[what]"
start_9692260a		He sulks like a schoolboy—a far cry from the terror of our first meeting.	game/script.rpy	1084	"[what]"
start_fc184f5e		I wonder how old he really is... He looks to be my age, but there’s no way to tell with apparitions.	game/script.rpy	1085	"[what]"
start_90c94344	e	I’ll be gone as soon as you escort me back to the light side of the barrier—it's not like I'm here for my own enjoyment.	game/script.rpy	1090	e "[what]"
start_c7ca17be	e	It won’t even be light out anymore at this rate! You’re taking up all my free time...	game/script.rpy	1094	e "[what]"
start_1b3d73a6	l	I {i}was{/i} considering cutting you some slack tomorrow until your... physical insubordination.	game/script.rpy	1099	l "[what]"
start_f10046c7		He links his hand to mine so we can once again cross the boundary.	game/script.rpy	1100	"[what]"
start_a99cf731	e	We’re partners! On equal footing! Something like this is nothing. In fact, it’s only the beginning of Edelweiss emancipation.	game/script.rpy	1104	e "[what]"
start_f3cb631c	e	For our next mission I’d say I deserve my own spider battalion, or squadron at the very least.	game/script.rpy	1108	e "[what]"
start_2c340fce	l	You can try to win their trust, hehe. But don't think they'll let you stage a mutiny.	game/script.rpy	1112	l "[what]"
start_c593939f	l	Their eyes are my eyes.	game/script.rpy	1116	l "[what]"
start_a2b44616	l	Now hush, let's move.	game/script.rpy	1119	l "[what]"
start_c4846d2c		The passage is less violent on my senses this time, but can’t quite be described as pleasant.	game/script.rpy	1128	"[what]"
start_a462b754		Perhaps with time I’ll get used to it.	game/script.rpy	1129	"[what]"
start_1354fbc4		My first foray into the beyond... I wouldn’t admit it out loud but without Lucifrid there I would have been terrified.	game/script.rpy	1130	"[what]"
start_98975845		The fear he instilled in me in our first meeting—I'm on the other side of that blade. At least for now.	game/script.rpy	1131	"[what]"
start_14b07e92		I'm learning and growing, perhaps more than a whole year of my father’s diviner tutoring could do for me.	game/script.rpy	1132	"[what]"
start_0b45412a		Are you proud, mother? Are you watching over me?	game/script.rpy	1133	"[what]"
start_1ae1acfb		Perhaps soon I’ll finally be like you.	game/script.rpy	1134	"[what]"
start_953ba315		Hmm?	game/script.rpy	1142	"[what]"
start_6cc60770		Now this is unusual. It seems like I’m the first one to arrive at our hideout.	game/script.rpy	1143	"[what]"
start_d83138c2		Almost two weeks have passed since my first meeting with the prince of spiders. I’ve settled into the rhythm of our after-school meetings.	game/script.rpy	1144	"[what]"
start_28fe70a1		I've learned that there's no escaping him while I'm on academy grounds. I've made my peace with it—I might as well go willingly.	game/script.rpy	1145	"[what]"
start_1ad7a338		I draw a small sigil on the blackboard in chalk, meant to draw out any apparitions in hiding.	game/script.rpy	1147	"[what]"
start_54b800d8		A number of spiders scurry out of their webs towards me, but Lucifrid is nowhere in sight.	game/script.rpy	1150	"[what]"
start_f5469fc2	e	Hello, little ones. Care to inform me of the location of your master?	game/script.rpy	1154	e "[what]"
start_b8265dec		Of course, the spiders don’t possess the gift of speech.	game/script.rpy	1155	"[what]"
start_5aff4c2a		Their unsettling, abundant gazes settle on me. I can’t quite shake the discomfort.	game/script.rpy	1156	"[what]"
start_be6f610a		While he’s out, I might as well take the opportunity for exposure therapy. We’re allies now, it won’t do to be afraid of them.	game/script.rpy	1157	"[what]"
start_4c1a9d18		I move closer to them and sit down on the floor, stretching out my arm.	game/script.rpy	1158	"[what]"
start_6db24e52		The spiders seem apprehensive about my intentions, perhaps they’re not used to acting outside their master’s orders.	game/script.rpy	1159	"[what]"
start_a3f9a614	e	Go forth! Tread upon me!	game/script.rpy	1163	e "[what]"
start_9c39e518		It worked! The spiders march in disciplined motion. Once they reach my shoulders I speak up once more.	game/script.rpy	1164	"[what]"
start_3b4098ed	e	Halt!	game/script.rpy	1165	e "[what]"
start_cda6039a		I nod in self-satisfaction. There’s nothing to be afraid of if they’ll listen to me.	game/script.rpy	1166	"[what]"
start_133b79e8	e	Gather on the desk and await further instruction.	game/script.rpy	1170	e "[what]"
start_b86e9e42		The spiders seem happy to obey me. It must be some effect of the contract between me and Lucifrid.	game/script.rpy	1171	"[what]"
start_60ab2270		Do we give off the same spiritual energy now? Is what's his also mine in equal measure? I wonder if I could summon other familiars too.	game/script.rpy	1172	"[what]"
start_b30f3cf3		But for now, I ought to focus on what's in front of me.	game/script.rpy	1173	"[what]"
start_9db47251		Interested in the spiders' abilities, I spend the next half hour testing out different commands.	game/script.rpy	1174	"[what]"
start_c927985c		They’ll happily spin webs to coat substances, or create bridges. They can create sturdy threads or sharp threads, depending on the occasion.	game/script.rpy	1175	"[what]"
start_2237ec7a		I want to know what their bite does, but without a target, that will have to wait. They refuse to fight each other at any rate.	game/script.rpy	1176	"[what]"
start_6fb387fb		Tiring of the serious exercise, I remember the candy in my pocket and offer it as a prize in various spider contests.	game/script.rpy	1177	"[what]"
start_cd109911		Climbing, running, jumping, spinning the longest threads, or the fastest webs. They're eager to win my approval.	game/script.rpy	1178	"[what]"
start_f9aba670	e	You did well, little Yang.	game/script.rpy	1179	e "[what]"
start_3898c26b		I pet the favoured child, fastest runner of the cohort, and give him his well-earned reward.	game/script.rpy	1180	"[what]"
start_59a6247f		Footsteps. My hair stands on end. An apparition...?	game/script.rpy	1184	"[what]"
start_be748142		But there is nothing to be afraid of.	game/script.rpy	1185	"[what]"
start_069ff761	e	Yang battalion, apprehend the intruder!	game/script.rpy	1189	e "[what]"
start_f1366b34		The spiders rush behind me and shoot their strings.	game/script.rpy	1192	"[what]"
start_f3af0265	l	I leave you alone for one afternoon and you’ve turned my followers against me already?!	game/script.rpy	1196	l "[what]"
start_92a67488	l	A wily one, this assistant.	game/script.rpy	1200	l "[what]"
start_0720760d	l	I guess the mutiny isn't far off!	game/script.rpy	1201	l "[what]"
start_0dd0d8e1		His tone feigns annoyance but I can tell he’s more impressed than anything.	game/script.rpy	1202	"[what]"
start_d42bc961	e	Lucifrid! You’re late!	game/script.rpy	1206	e "[what]"
start_67e0a9e6	l	I’m happy you missed me! Now please, help me get this mess off.	game/script.rpy	1209	l "[what]"
start_9b78640f		He motions at the silky substance coating his clothes. Well, I guess that {i}was{/i} my fault.	game/script.rpy	1210	"[what]"
start_264d6616	l	Today I’ve tidied up most of our task for us.	game/script.rpy	1219	l "[what]"
start_f4f8fa72	l	Here.	game/script.rpy	1223	l "[what]"
start_cffb6ddd		Lucifrid presents me with a tiny bird slumped in his palm, barely breathing.	game/script.rpy	1224	"[what]"
start_3fb87784		He doesn’t need to explain, this must be the weakened form of one of the apparitions in his domain.	game/script.rpy	1225	"[what]"
start_947dd89e		Many apparitions have various forms, the more intricate forms becoming impossible to maintain as they lose power.	game/script.rpy	1226	"[what]"
start_b8a89ead		I wonder if Lucifrid manifests himself in different ways; this form doesn’t seem too strenuous in upkeep.	game/script.rpy	1227	"[what]"
start_9f35daef		I've gotten used to helping him by now. I lend my assistance in various ways: sometimes it's a fight like the ice spirit, sometimes it's nothing more than using his tome to administer the final rites. Like now.	game/script.rpy	1228	"[what]"
start_c9cbe487		Drawing upon a larger sigil inscribed in one of the desks, I manifest the spider prince’s tome.	game/script.rpy	1232	"[what]"
start_4164d2a2	extend 	 Its pages scramble open as I recite the incantation.	game/script.rpy	1234	extend "[what]"
start_2e0a6206	e2	State thy name and thine allegiance be manifest.	game/script.rpy	1235	e2 "[what]"
start_14596e06		The bird croaks something indeterminate, though the tome does not discriminate.	game/script.rpy	1236	"[what]"
start_341a4524		Laid to rest on the page, the bird’s physical form fades and the abandoned classroom quiets down once more.	game/script.rpy	1237	"[what]"
start_6a08a80e	l	Well done, my dear assistant. It seems a reward is in order!	game/script.rpy	1242	l "[what]"
start_59a7cc15		Lucifrid pats my head. I don't resist, just wear my most unimpressed expression. Choose your battles.	game/script.rpy	1243	"[what]"
start_3ad5b9f6	e	Alright! Let’s go get ice cream!	game/script.rpy	1247	e "[what]"
start_0c54c343	l	You’re aware I can’t leave school grounds?	game/script.rpy	1251	l "[what]"
start_e8a98cda	e	There’s a vending machine in the gardens, you’ve never used it?	game/script.rpy	1255	e "[what]"
start_27eacc74	l	I have greater concerns than sweet treats.	game/script.rpy	1259	l "[what]"
start_db565b41	e	Hehe, seems there are some things the humble Edelweiss can teach our dark overlord.	game/script.rpy	1263	e "[what]"
start_bd5ef23f		The two of us sit down on a bench in the courtyard, ice cream in hand, basking in the last rays of sun of a clement summer afternoon.	game/script.rpy	1269	"[what]"
start_7f43d84c		The breeze rustles through the trees, obscuring quiet snippets of conversation between students on their way home.	game/script.rpy	1270	"[what]"
start_dbaf49dc		I don’t think anyone is paying attention, but I speak quietly regardless. If I’m talking to the air, I should at least be subtle about it.	game/script.rpy	1271	"[what]"
start_01234255	e	My father has been quite impressed with me lately. Unsurprisingly, practical experience teaches more about diviner business than the classroom ever could.	game/script.rpy	1275	e "[what]"
start_438204a3	e	Well, I didn't mention the cause for the sudden improvement. That would probably impress him less...	game/script.rpy	1279	e "[what]"
start_58cf75a9	l	Is that what concerns you? Your father’s opinion?	game/script.rpy	1283	l "[what]"
start_d60efce7		Lucifrid sounds disdainful, as if the very idea of seeking another person’s approval is an affront.	game/script.rpy	1284	"[what]"
start_587f4098	e	Well, it’s not just that! I want to be a great diviner for my own sake!	game/script.rpy	1288	e "[what]"
start_2797e8bc	l	Does it afford you power and status in human society?	game/script.rpy	1292	l "[what]"
start_86963fc4	e	Hmm... Not exactly.	game/script.rpy	1293	e "[what]"
start_47287903	e	Most people don’t even know about apparitions so it’s not like there’s anything to brag about. But it’s in my family’s blood, it’s our honorable duty.	game/script.rpy	1294	e "[what]"
start_a77b7783	e	My mother was one of the most powerful diviners to ever live, I have to live up to her name!	game/script.rpy	1298	e "[what]"
start_a421ca7a		Lucifrid looks into the distance—one of the first times he hasn’t had a quip at the ready.	game/script.rpy	1299	"[what]"
start_6aa91d62	l	I think duty is something you have to give shape for yourself.	game/script.rpy	1303	l "[what]"
start_51d12f6d	l	No one can know what anyone else is truly thinking or feeling.	game/script.rpy	1304	l "[what]"
start_3649a7bd	l	Your mother, your whole lineage, who knows what any of them were actually doing it for? It’s just your projection.	game/script.rpy	1305	l "[what]"
start_d0c325ea	l	The only thing you can trust is your own gut, and the only one who needs to be pleased with your actions is yourself.	game/script.rpy	1307	l "[what]"
start_331837ce	l	It’s a fool’s errand to try and live up to the expectations of forces outside your understanding.	game/script.rpy	1308	l "[what]"
start_b404fb8b	l	If someone doesn’t like what you’re doing, you just have to become strong enough that they can’t begin to object.	game/script.rpy	1309	l "[what]"
start_ab59e272		His tone is uncharacteristically serious, but before I can comment, he switches back,	game/script.rpy	1312	"[what]"
start_65905003	extend 	 making a show of grasping his ice cream wrapper and crushing it like an insect.	game/script.rpy	1314	extend "[what]"
start_b6f0cdc9	e	Yes, I think I’ll do just that!	game/script.rpy	1322	e evening smile "[what]"
start_39c30f45	e	I’ll grow my powers in secret until the day I can overthrow you and be free of our contract once and for all.	game/script.rpy	1323	e evening smug "[what]"
start_357e36cd	l	You’re stuck in my web, my dear assistant. There’s no way out of it unless I wish it so.	game/script.rpy	1326	l "[what]"
start_5351275d	l	And the more you resist... the more you get stuck.	game/script.rpy	1328	l "[what]"
start_1660652c	l	Don’t even dream of challenging me at my own game.	game/script.rpy	1330	l "[what]"
start_71d4d447		He laughs and I shiver. I keep getting too comfortable around him. No matter how affable he acts, he’s not my friend.	game/script.rpy	1331	"[what]"
start_ff04dc2a	e	It’s easy to say all that when you’re an apparition with no concept of family or kin.	game/script.rpy	1337	e evening "[what]"
start_3b7ce989	e	If I do as you say, I’ll end up like you! Alone, with my only company someone who wouldn’t be there if I hadn’t twisted their arm into it.	game/script.rpy	1338	e "[what]"
start_821dd2d9	l	Ah yes, truly the worst of all fates. I’ll have you know I’m quite happy with my life.	game/script.rpy	1340	l "[what]"
start_934b4f18	e	Well, I’m happy for you, but I wouldn’t be! I need other people.	game/script.rpy	1341	e evening conflicted "[what]"
start_f13563da	e	And if I have to sacrifice some of my personal desires to keep them around, that’s more than worth it to me.	game/script.rpy	1342	e evening rueful "[what]"
start_0dca174d	l	Alright! As long as you’re sacrificing your personal desires for {i}me{/i} I won’t complain, ehehe.	game/script.rpy	1344	l "[what]"
start_ca86f10b	e	If I’m going to do what {i}I{/i} want, then I at least have to know what that is...	game/script.rpy	1350	e evening awkward "[what]"
start_e64fa2fd		Lucifrid looks at me incredulously. Like it’s the first time he’s considered the possibility of someone having no strong desire of their own.	game/script.rpy	1352	"[what]"
start_d8c1eaeb		His confused face transforms into a grin, until he bursts into earnest laughter.	game/script.rpy	1353	"[what]"
start_31b97668	l	Ahahahaha!	game/script.rpy	1355	l "[what]"
start_34b0c97c	e	Wow, hey, I can take abuse, but no laughing at me! You’re horrible!	game/script.rpy	1356	e evening angry "[what]"
start_5a352bd5	l	Haha...ha... it’s your fault for saying something so absurd.	game/script.rpy	1357	l "[what]"
start_36df077f	l	Well, you were right, there are some things you can still teach me. Humans truly are mystifying.	game/script.rpy	1359	l "[what]"
start_e755445c		I frown at him. He doesn’t have to be so rude... but maybe he has a point.	game/script.rpy	1360	"[what]"
start_70eadca5	e	I’ll let you know once I’ve found it. That something I want.	game/script.rpy	1361	e evening neutral "[what]"
start_3674d480	l	Who knows, if you’re a good little assistant, I might even help you achieve it.	game/script.rpy	1362	l "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_be5c0c54		Dusk begins to set in, and without my noticing, the school grounds have grown deserted.	game/script.rpy	1370	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_3809fa38		Lucifrid gets up, stretches his arms and yawns. Eating ice cream is a tiring affair.	game/script.rpy	1371	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_0e9ef8f2	e	My liege, might I have your permission to head home for the day?	game/script.rpy	1375	e "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_15d4b8c8		He gives a curt nod, befitting a noble of his station.	game/script.rpy	1379	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_a47399ff	l	For today you are dismissed.	game/script.rpy	1383	l "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_606b5b6e		I salute him and give a bow.	game/script.rpy	1384	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_a7640242		We slip in and out of our roles with aplomb. Everything is a game, but I am worried for the day when it won't be.	game/script.rpy	1385	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_2b623732		As I walk home, the topic of our discussion lingers in my mind.	game/script.rpy	1392	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_3bd556c2		The idea of what I want has always been blurry. To begin with, the person I am is the sum of what everyone else thinks or hopes or expects of me.	game/script.rpy	1393	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_cb7b825f		Isn't that how everyone is?	game/script.rpy	1394	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_1ecce103		We start with something, but then we're reflected in the mirrors of other people's eyes, and we model ourselves on that reflection.	game/script.rpy	1395	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_5e1182d2		We rebel against it, conform to it, or endlessly negotiate between the two.	game/script.rpy	1396	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_d4d4ec75		It's an eternal recursion of interpretation and reinterpretation. Who can distinguish what the original was?	game/script.rpy	1397	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_9978bc7d		The first people we look to are our family. For as long as I can remember, I've looked up to mother.	game/script.rpy	1398	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_91deb8fa		Everyone loved her, trusted her, believed in her. And so did I.	game/script.rpy	1399	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_4735f6b3		If I could be like her, my father wouldn't need to worry anymore. I know he misses her.	game/script.rpy	1400	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_32321052		I could protect my brother, if I were just a little more reliable.	game/script.rpy	1401	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_5e728363		All the same, I know I can't be her. But why won't anyone let me try? Why doesn't father trust me with any responsibility?	game/script.rpy	1402	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_77848632		All I want is to prove myself—prove that I'm worthy of that same love and trust and belief.	game/script.rpy	1403	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_c8acfb6d		Maybe I can show them. If I can handle Lucifrid, they'll have to see that I'm competent. Something good will come of this. It simply has to.	game/script.rpy	1404	"[what]"
