postchoice_lucycourtyard_524f7fa2	i	Our parents have their reasons, I’m sure. There have been... disagreements in the past.{nw=1.5}	game/script.rpy	1685	i stiff sigh "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_35943173	extend i	 But there is no reason for us to carry on their feud.	game/script.rpy	1687	extend "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_921068b1	i	We share a duty to protect the human realm from the beyond, wouldn’t you agree?	game/script.rpy	1688	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_7722e85f	i	But we can’t do that without first keeping ourselves safe.	game/script.rpy	1690	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_69e83b01		He pauses and my initial excitement chills down to a freezing temperature.	game/script.rpy	1691	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_9e7d7092	i	You’ve been beset by one of {i}them{/i}, haven’t you?	game/script.rpy	1693	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_3a67eeff		A sinking feeling settles in my stomach, and I don’t know how to respond.	game/script.rpy	1694	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_88c698b5		If this is a game, I have no cards in hand and the board is firmly under his control.	game/script.rpy	1695	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_638b51d9		But if he is my ally, why do I feel so threatened?	game/script.rpy	1696	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_4feca0f2		I need more time to think through my moves. Why is Emrys always right?! Though what good would it do if he were here...	game/script.rpy	1697	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_7faffd96		I haven’t even decided what to do about Lucifrid yet, so I can’t involve anyone else. Let alone a complete stranger.	game/script.rpy	1698	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_08156e84		Ilya may be an exorcist, but who knows if he can best the prince of spiders? And if he can’t, I’m the one who takes the fall.	game/script.rpy	1699	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_75760071	e	I have done nothing outside my own volition. You don’t need to concern yourself with me.	game/script.rpy	1700	e determined "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_f83bd5c0		His eyes turn to pity now. Oh, that look pisses me off.	game/script.rpy	1702	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_ef76a3f0	i	I cannot allow an apparition of his calibre to exert influence over the light side of the barrier. You understand that, don’t you?	game/script.rpy	1703	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_83f42ba9	i	That thing needs to be eliminated. For your good as well.	game/script.rpy	1704	i stiff cold "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_935848d0	i	In fact, perhaps I should have started off by thanking you. For bringing this existence to my attention. It has lowered its guard around you, it appears.	game/script.rpy	1705	i cold_smile "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_f3437214		Eliminate Lucifrid? If anyone’s doing that it’ll be me. And it would be a last resort.	game/script.rpy	1714	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_9cffe8f3		I’m a diviner, we protect the balance across the boundary. It would be a gross overstepping of our duties to eliminate without searching for a more peaceful resolution.	game/script.rpy	1715	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_c8c717b6		We’re supposed to help breed understanding, not hatred!	game/script.rpy	1716	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_5ead167a		I doubt he'll be convinced by diviner philosophy anytime soon. I’ll have a better chance convincing him to back off by using his own terms. Force against force.	game/script.rpy	1717	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_27fbade3	e	I should thank you too, for opening up to me and letting me know I’m not as alone as I assumed in this school!	game/script.rpy	1718	e smile "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_f612fcce	e	However, I think you should know better than to meddle in diviner affairs. I may still be in training, but that doesn’t mean I can’t handle my own.	game/script.rpy	1720	e determined "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_983269ab	e	The spider boy is under my control, and I will deal with him as needed.	game/script.rpy	1721	e neutral "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_381facbd	e	He hasn’t posed a threat to the students, and as long as he’s willing to help keep other apparitions in check I’d say antagonising him would only be going against our own objectives.	game/script.rpy	1722	e "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_df612e78	e	So thank you, but no thank you. If the situation changes, I’ll keep your offer in mind.	game/script.rpy	1723	e smile "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_751950e0		Checkmate, Ilya.	game/script.rpy	1724	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_dad59eb1		Did I embroider the truth a little to strengthen my point? Sure. Did I embroider it a lot? Okay, maybe.	game/script.rpy	1725	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_e8b9a160		But there’s nothing he can say now that won’t make him seem reckless and hasty.	game/script.rpy	1726	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_2a343ff5	i	I see. Perhaps I have underestimated you indeed. But I assure you it was with the best of intentions that I approached you.	game/script.rpy	1728	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_3c94fb6c	i	I would hate to see you in trouble. If anything concerns you, please don’t hesitate to confide in me.	game/script.rpy	1730	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_00f3d527		Ilya means me no harm, he’s acting out of concern for me even if we may not agree on our methods.	game/script.rpy	1736	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_e8d08349		Diviners facilitate peaceful coexistence with the beyond, keeping both sides of the barrier in harmony, balanced like two sides of a scale.	game/script.rpy	1737	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_cef4738b		Exorcists are guardians of the human realm, and will do what they must even at the detriment of apparitions.	game/script.rpy	1738	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_8069b2e3		Isn’t there some way for us to see eye to eye?	game/script.rpy	1739	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_8024bb1f	e	Ilya... Thank you for telling me all this. I never knew there were others I could confide in about the dark side of this school.	game/script.rpy	1740	e conflicted "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_11b8a42d	e	Truthfully, I’m still learning every day about the apparitions and their ways, but I want to respect the legacy of my mother and her belief in our peaceful coexistence.	game/script.rpy	1742	e rueful "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_8a50875a	e	I can’t condone exorcising Lucifrid, even if he may interfere with my life. {nw=1.5}	game/script.rpy	1743	e neutral "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_ea5e11f8	extend e	Being annoying isn’t a sin!	game/script.rpy	1745	extend "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_ed56623d	e	I have faith that I can convince him to leave the student body in peace, so won’t you give me some time?	game/script.rpy	1746	e smile "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_ebe9425f	i	So he calls himself Lucifrid...	game/script.rpy	1748	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_13c9f74d	i	You can’t let your guard down around these creatures, Edelweiss. They’re not like us, no matter how similar their forms may appear.	game/script.rpy	1750	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_ed889237	i	Don't make the mistake of expecting reason or empathy from them.	game/script.rpy	1751	i sigh "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_7d932ed3	i	But I am not your enemy. I will watch over you from a distance then, but know that I won’t hesitate to act if he proves to be a threat to you or any other student.	game/script.rpy	1753	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_928b737e		I wouldn’t let Lucifrid know but... in a way, he’s finally made me feel useful. He's given me what my father refused me: a chance to prove myself.	game/script.rpy	1760	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_43c82131		There’s a task that only I can fulfill by his side, and if anyone is going to take that away, it’s going to be me.	game/script.rpy	1761	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_dfe5de95		Ilya doesn’t know anything about our contract, he doesn’t know anything about Lucifrid, and he doesn’t know anything about me.	game/script.rpy	1762	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_e9f41691		How could he claim to be on my side? He’s only fulfilling his own goals and trying to manipulate me into doing his bidding.	game/script.rpy	1763	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_146e602e		Well, is Lucifrid any different? Maybe not.	game/script.rpy	1764	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_1da568a4		But at least I know that devil.	game/script.rpy	1765	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_300a7d60		Lucifrid has never been ambiguous about his questionable goals, he’s easier to trust than someone who claims to be "helping" me with a chillingly cold smile on their face.	game/script.rpy	1766	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_e70a23b3	e	Aren’t you misunderstanding something? The spider prince and I are allies. Why on earth would I agree to let you exorcise him?	game/script.rpy	1767	e angry "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_efa484d5	e	Diviners and exorcists clearly operate differently, and you will not force your crude methods upon me.	game/script.rpy	1768	e "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_552376e9	e	I don’t care to make an enemy of you, but if you lay a hand on my partner, I will be forced to act.	game/script.rpy	1769	e determined "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_a4c3167f		Ilya’s carefully controlled demeanour cracks as I veritably {i}hear{/i} him grit his teeth.	game/script.rpy	1771	"[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_743ac903	i	You’ve clearly wasted no time in choosing the company you keep. Perhaps a measure of discernment would have served you better.	game/script.rpy	1772	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_8288088c	i	I have your best interests at heart, please remember that. I have years of experience dealing with the beyond, perhaps my knowledge might serve you one day.	game/script.rpy	1773	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_b8d8578e	i	But rest assured, I have no interest in making enemies today either. This was merely my first warning.	game/script.rpy	1775	i "[what]"
postchoice_lucycourtyard_2e1bdba7	e	Consider your warning received. I hope mine was as well.	game/script.rpy	1776	e smile "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_026f4301		Ilya and I shake hands. I can’t tell if we're allies or enemies—it seems we may be both.	game/script.rpy	1783	"[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_c48810f7	e	I should probably let you know, I told Emrys we're dating.	game/script.rpy	1784	e neutral slightblush "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_5bf2ce6b		Did Ilya twitch a little?	game/script.rpy	1790	"[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_f2987dda	i	Emrys?	game/script.rpy	1791	i stiff calm "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_ee889495	e	...My assistant. I can't let him find out about the spider apparition.	game/script.rpy	1792	e neutral none "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_26bd44b8	i	Have you told anyone else about this?	game/script.rpy	1793	i "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_de120c15	e	No. Just him. He was more than happy to assume we don't want your admirers on my case.	game/script.rpy	1794	e "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_ae80b813	i	I—	game/script.rpy	1795	i sigh "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_1f686e71		He sighs, though he tries to make even this movement swift and dignified. His discomfort is palpable in the air.	game/script.rpy	1796	"[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_5746f13d	i	If we’ll be seeing more of each other soon, I suppose this is a fine cover story.	game/script.rpy	1797	i calm "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_3e965b68	i	I’ll play along with your ruse. You’re free to tell who you like, though it may do more harm than good.	game/script.rpy	1798	i "[what]"
postchoice_ilyameeting_ce153295	i	I’ll trust your judgment on the matter. I can’t claim to be an expert on... girl politics.	game/script.rpy	1799	i polite sigh "[what]"
